{"event": "model_request", "time": 1793846791.8479624, "run_id": "78c4b7e42755425f995f878c420c69d8", "seq": 5, "number": 1, "body": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Complete the task using the Python tools below.\nReturn ONE JSON object with string fields \"thought\" (next action) and \"code\" (executable Python), then STOP.\nExample: {\"thought\":\"Check progress.\",\"code\":\"print(task_status())\"}\nNo Markdown fences, extra JSON, simulated observations or future turns. Keep the action within the output budget.\n\n\nCall tools with keyword arguments. Arrays are Python lists ['a','b'], never encoded strings.\nReads return dicts: r['content'] is text, r['file_hash'] is the edit hash. Commands return r['rc'] and r['stdout'].\nUse print() for needed output. Group independent operations. Variables and imports persist; successful statements\nbefore an error remain executed. Correct the error without restarting completed work.\n\nPaths are relative to the task repository; '.' is its root. Omit cwd for commands there.\nUse tools for all file/command operations. Edit only allowed files, never tests. Use current file_hash as expected_hash.\nImports allowed: ['collections', 'datetime', 'itertools', 'json', 'math', 'queue', 'random', 're', 'stat', 'statistics', 'time', 'unicodedata']; import before use.\nRead sufficient evidence, preserve relevant findings when useful, implement and verify. Avoid repeated unchanged reads.\nCall final_answer when ready: it runs missing current-version checks, finishes the plan on success,\nor returns the actual failure for repair. A successful test and final_answer may share one action.\n\nAvailable tools:\n```python\ndef list_files(path: string, limit: integer, offset: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"List text files under a repository path.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        limit: limit\n        offset: offset\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef search_code(query: string, paths: array, limit: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Search visible text source files for a literal string.\n\n    Args:\n        query: query\n        paths: paths\n        limit: limit\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_file(path: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a text file in full. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids. Read result['content'], not result[:N].\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_range(path: string, start_line: integer, end_line: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read an inclusive line range from a text file. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        start_line: start line\n        end_line: end line\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_symbol(path: string, symbol: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a complete Python class or function including decorators. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        symbol: symbol\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_file(path: string, content: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Replace an editable text file after checking its current hash.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        content: content\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef replace_text_batch(path: string, edits: array, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Atomically replace unique nonoverlapping occurrences from one file version. Returns ok, path, before_hash, file_hash, changed.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        edits: Python list of objects, e.g. [{'old_text':'before','new_text':'after'}]; all refer to the original file.\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef run_command(argv: array, cwd: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use '.' for the task repository root. argv is a Python list[str]. Returns dict: rc, stdout (text), stderr, timed_out.\n\n    Args:\n        argv: argv\n        cwd: cwd\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef update_plan(items: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Set the task plan; preserve titles/order and update todo/doing/done.\n\n    Args:\n        items: List of objects, e.g. [{\"title\":\"Read sources\",\"status\":\"doing\"}]. Each status is todo, doing or done; retain existing titles/order.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef recall(evidence_ids: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Queue evidence ids; batches are bounded and overflow remains pending.\n\n    Args:\n        evidence_ids: evidence ids\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef task_status() -> object:\n    \"\"\"Show the current plan, remaining reading, notes, changes and verification, plus evidence ids.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_note(title: string, content: string, evidence_ids: array, section: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence.\n\n    Args:\n        title: Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\n        content: One contiguous string literal, 20..3000 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\n        evidence_ids: Python list[str], e.g. ['ev-abc'], not a string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n        section: Optional stable note key; source notes still allow 20..3000 characters.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nComplete the requested local task.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"source\", \"editable\": [\"data.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"data.py\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 3}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\nWhen calling write_note, put the complete exact note text in the thought field, then pass that same text as one content string literal in code. This preserves a contiguous model-authored copy through JSON/Python escaping.\nRead all three files with read_file first, then read/reuse complete mechanisms from all three\nbefore the first edit. Source notes are OPTIONAL; current source blocks can be used directly.\nWhen progress says phase=edit, the initial reading and baseline are satisfied. Apply a scoped edit and verify.\nA note may replace original text only after its mechanisms were exposed. Do not repeat full reads to register them again.\n\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"baseline\",\"next_requirement\":\"baseline: python -m pytest -q\",\"remaining_count\":4,\"requests_left\":2,\"baseline_done\":0,\"changed_files\":[],\"verified_current\":0,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":1,\"max_requests\":3,\"requests_after_response\":2,\"first_write_reading_required\":true,\"full_reads_registered\":{},\"evidence_delivery\":\"Registered full reads are logged tool reads; Evidence headers show selected ranges, whose delivery requires HTTP confirmation.\",\"required_mechanisms_exposed\":{}}"}]}], "model": "deepseek-flash", "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "stop": ["Observation:", "Calling tools:"]}, "chars": 7498, "content_chars": 6973, "course_content_chars": 7327}
