imit: limit\n        offset: offset\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef search_code(query: string, paths: array, limit: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Search visible text source files for a literal string.\n\n    Args:\n        query: query\n        paths: paths\n        limit: limit\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_file(path: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a text file in full. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids. Read result['content'], not result[:N].\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_range(path: string, start_line: integer, end_line: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read an inclusive line range from a text file. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        start_line: start line\n        end_line: end line\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_symbol(path: string, symbol: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a complete Python class or function including decorators. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        symbol: symbol\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_file(path: string, content: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Replace an editable text file after checking its current hash.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        content: content\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef replace_text_batch(path: string, edits: array, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Atomically replace unique nonoverlapping occurrences from one file version. Returns ok, path, before_hash, file_hash, changed.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        edits: Python list of objects, e.g. [{'old_text':'before','new_text':'after'}]; all refer to the original file.\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef run_command(argv: array, cwd: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use '.' for the task repository root. argv is a Python list[str]. Returns dict: rc, stdout (text), stderr, timed_out.\n\n